      "latest_changelog": "<h2 data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"26\">RP NPCs &mdash; v0.5.0 (Beta)</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"28\" data-end=\"206\">This one&rsquo;s chunky. Still beta, still evolving fast &mdash; but <strong data-start=\"85\" data-end=\"94\">0.5.0</strong> adds a pile of new powers, better organization tools, and a few &ldquo;please stop being immortal by accident&rdquo; fixes.</p>\r\n<h3 data-start=\"208\" data-end=\"234\">New Features &amp; Changes</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"236\" data-end=\"4040\">\r\n<li data-start=\"236\" data-end=\"568\">\r\n<p data-start=\"238\" data-end=\"568\"><strong data-start=\"238\" data-end=\"283\">Player-Specific Flags (Non-Global Flags!)</strong><br data-start=\"283\" data-end=\"286\" />Flags can now be <strong data-start=\"305\" data-end=\"319\">per-player</strong> instead of global. Use <code data-start=\"343\" data-end=\"353\">[player]</code> bracket syntax in the flag name (as the full name or a prefix) and the flag is stored on the <em data-start=\"447\" data-end=\"455\">player</em> instead of the NPC.<br data-start=\"475\" data-end=\"478\" />Great for &ldquo;this NPC remembers <em data-start=\"510\" data-end=\"515\">you</em> said X&rdquo; without turning it into server-wide reality.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"570\" data-end=\"862\">\r\n<p data-start=\"572\" data-end=\"727\"><strong data-start=\"572\" data-end=\"626\">Languages Split from Factions + BASICs Integration</strong><br data-start=\"626\" data-end=\"629\" />Languages are now <strong data-start=\"649\" data-end=\"676\">independent of factions</strong>, and they now integrate with <strong data-start=\"706\" data-end=\"720\">The BASICs</strong> mod.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"730\" data-end=\"862\">\r\n<li data-start=\"730\" data-end=\"776\">\r\n<p data-start=\"732\" data-end=\"776\">Works <strong data-start=\"738\" data-end=\"757\">with or without</strong> BASICs installed</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"779\" data-end=\"862\">\r\n<p data-start=\"781\" data-end=\"862\">If BASICs is present, RP NPCs will recognize and use any languages BASICs defines</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"864\" data-end=\"1080\">\r\n<p data-start=\"866\" data-end=\"1080\"><strong data-start=\"866\" data-end=\"920\">Import/Export NPC Coordinates (Clipboard-Friendly)</strong><br data-start=\"920\" data-end=\"923\" />You can now <strong data-start=\"937\" data-end=\"976\">export an NPC&rsquo;s coordinates to JSON</strong> (and import them back). Copy/paste waypoint setups without retyping coordinates like a medieval scribe.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1082\" data-end=\"1276\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1084\" data-end=\"1276\"><strong data-start=\"1084\" data-end=\"1118\">Time &amp; Date Sensitive Dialogue</strong><br data-start=\"1118\" data-end=\"1121\" />Dialogue can now be <strong data-start=\"1143\" data-end=\"1161\">time-sensitive</strong> and <strong data-start=\"1166\" data-end=\"1184\">date-sensitive</strong>, so you can do seasonal lines, timed events, or &ldquo;only on the feast day&rdquo; style interactions.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1278\" data-end=\"1515\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1280\" data-end=\"1515\"><strong data-start=\"1280\" data-end=\"1338\">Relative Coordinates with <code data-start=\"1308\" data-end=\"1311\">~</code> (Minecraft-style sanity)</strong><br data-start=\"1338\" data-end=\"1341\" />Coordinates can now be relative using a leading <code data-start=\"1391\" data-end=\"1394\">~</code> &mdash; offsets from the NPC&rsquo;s current position, positive or negative.<br data-start=\"1459\" data-end=\"1462\" />(Your waypoint editing just got much less painful.)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1517\" data-end=\"1819\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1519\" data-end=\"1819\"><strong data-start=\"1519\" data-end=\"1564\">Wake Up NPC Action (Stop Talking to Beds)</strong><br data-start=\"1564\" data-end=\"1567\" />If an NPC is sleeping, dialogue can now include an action to <strong data-start=\"1630\" data-end=\"1655\">force them to wake up</strong>.<br data-start=\"1656\" data-end=\"1659\" />You can also <strong data-start=\"1674\" data-end=\"1682\">gate</strong> this behind a dialogue option.<br data-start=\"1713\" data-end=\"1716\" />If you don&rsquo;t use Wake Up: NPCs will still talk from bed like a tired innkeeper who refuses to sit up.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1821\" data-end=\"2037\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1823\" data-end=\"2037\"><strong data-start=\"1823\" data-end=\"1858\">Persistent NPCs (Chunk Anchors)</strong><br data-start=\"1858\" data-end=\"1861\" />NPCs can be made <strong data-start=\"1880\" data-end=\"1894\">persistent</strong>, meaning they keep their chunks loaded while they&rsquo;re in them.<br data-start=\"1956\" data-end=\"1959\" />Useful for NPCs actively working an area (harvesting routes, patrols, etc.).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2039\" data-end=\"2264\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2041\" data-end=\"2264\"><strong data-start=\"2041\" data-end=\"2087\">Faction Relations System + Management View</strong><br data-start=\"2087\" data-end=\"2090\" />NPC factions can now have <strong data-start=\"2118\" data-end=\"2139\">hostile relations</strong> with each other, with a new view for managing it.<br data-start=\"2189\" data-end=\"2192\" />Hostile factions treat each other as hostile entities, as they should.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2266\" data-end=\"2663\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2268\" data-end=\"2363\"><strong data-start=\"2268\" data-end=\"2313\">Player &harr; NPC / Faction Relationship Scale</strong><br data-start=\"2313\" data-end=\"2316\" />Players now have relationship standings with:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2366\" data-end=\"2663\">\r\n<li data-start=\"2366\" data-end=\"2446\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2368\" data-end=\"2446\"><strong data-start=\"2368\" data-end=\"2387\">Individual NPCs</strong>: from <strong data-start=\"2394\" data-end=\"2418\">Neutral &rarr; Respectful</strong>, or <strong data-start=\"2423\" data-end=\"2446\">Neutral &rarr; Resentful</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2449\" data-end=\"2663\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2451\" data-end=\"2663\"><strong data-start=\"2451\" data-end=\"2463\">Factions</strong>: from <strong data-start=\"2470\" data-end=\"2491\">Neutral &rarr; Favored</strong> or <strong data-start=\"2495\" data-end=\"2519\">Neutral &rarr; Disfavored</strong><br data-start=\"2519\" data-end=\"2522\" />Players can become <strong data-start=\"2543\" data-end=\"2554\">members</strong> via dialogue, and yes &mdash; <strong data-start=\"2579\" data-end=\"2636\">killing an NPC can make you hostile to their faction.</strong> Consequences have arrived.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2665\" data-end=\"2912\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2667\" data-end=\"2912\"><strong data-start=\"2667\" data-end=\"2717\">Clutter Items Should Keep Their Type (Mostly&hellip;)</strong><br data-start=\"2717\" data-end=\"2720\" />Clutter items <em data-start=\"2736\" data-end=\"2744\">should</em> now maintain their correct type. Big <strong data-start=\"2782\" data-end=\"2792\">should</strong>.<br data-start=\"2793\" data-end=\"2796\" />Some cases still misbehave &mdash; please report bugs if clutter stops responding correctly for trading or quest checks.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2914\" data-end=\"3245\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2916\" data-end=\"3044\"><strong data-start=\"2916\" data-end=\"2966\">NPC Health Defaults Fixed + Immortality Button</strong><br data-start=\"2966\" data-end=\"2969\" />NPC health is now editable, and defaults have been brought back to earth:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3047\" data-end=\"3245\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3047\" data-end=\"3100\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3049\" data-end=\"3100\">Default health is now <strong data-start=\"3071\" data-end=\"3080\">20 HP</strong> (instead of 1000)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3103\" data-end=\"3245\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3105\" data-end=\"3245\">&ldquo;Immortal&rdquo; button sets <strong data-start=\"3128\" data-end=\"3139\">1000 HP</strong> + <strong data-start=\"3142\" data-end=\"3163\">1000 HP/sec regen</strong><br data-start=\"3163\" data-end=\"3166\" />Technically killable, but only if you commit war crimes against the engine.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3247\" data-end=\"3434\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3249\" data-end=\"3321\"><strong data-start=\"3249\" data-end=\"3286\">Death, Looting, and Despawn Timer</strong><br data-start=\"3286\" data-end=\"3289\" />NPCs can now <strong data-start=\"3304\" data-end=\"3311\">die</strong>. If dead:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3324\" data-end=\"3434\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3324\" data-end=\"3348\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3326\" data-end=\"3348\">They can be <strong data-start=\"3338\" data-end=\"3348\">looted</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3351\" data-end=\"3434\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3353\" data-end=\"3434\">They will <strong data-start=\"3363\" data-end=\"3387\">despawn after 3 days</strong> (no more eternal corpses cluttering the world)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3436\" data-end=\"3613\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3438\" data-end=\"3613\"><strong data-start=\"3438\" data-end=\"3460\">UI Bloat Reduction</strong><br data-start=\"3460\" data-end=\"3463\" />Unused UI elements (like the older path system bits that weren&rsquo;t doing anything useful) have been removed to keep the mod leaner and less confusing.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3615\" data-end=\"3837\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3617\" data-end=\"3837\"><strong data-start=\"3617\" data-end=\"3668\">Appearance Menu Revamp (Full List, All Genders)</strong><br data-start=\"3668\" data-end=\"3671\" />The appearance menu now shows a <strong data-start=\"3705\" data-end=\"3743\">full list of available appearances</strong> for all NPCs, male and female.<br data-start=\"3774\" data-end=\"3777\" />Yes, you can pick whichever &ldquo;Nadia&rdquo; you want. No judgment.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3839\" data-end=\"4040\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3841\" data-end=\"3860\"><strong data-start=\"3841\" data-end=\"3860\">Better Defaults</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3863\" data-end=\"4040\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3863\" data-end=\"3915\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3865\" data-end=\"3915\">NPC equipment slots now default to <strong data-start=\"3900\" data-end=\"3915\">flint tools</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3918\" data-end=\"4040\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3920\" data-end=\"4040\">The <strong data-start=\"3924\" data-end=\"3938\">Reset Tree</strong> button now generates a much more useful <strong data-start=\"3979\" data-end=\"3998\">dialogue preset</strong> (less empty slate, more &ldquo;ready to build&rdquo;)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>",
      "is_symlink": false
    },
